wever, (consistent with prior theory in cultural stratification) that culture-mediated interaction is stratified by the same markers of social position (Age, Gender) and social status (Education) that previous research has shown also characterize audience
\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41  \hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 segmentation in the corresponding cultural domains. 
\par \hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 In particular, culture-talk in those domains characterized by large-scale commercial culture (Movies, Music) is strongly stratified by Age (with the young being more likely to use such culture in convers
\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 \hich\f41 ation) and Education (with the highly educated generating more culture-based talk). Culture-talk recruiting cultural knowledge from the higher-status \'93\loch\f41 \hich\f41 non-profit\'94\loch\f41 
