 is too sporadic and inconsistent a ph\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 e\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 nomenon with which to judge whether persons are connected or not (Bearman and Parigi 2004).
\par \hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 \hich\f41 A substantial number of people (including a larger proportion of married persons) report simply not having anybody with which to discuss \'93\loch\f41 \hich\f41 important\'94\loch\f41  matters with (B
\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 \hich\f41 earman and Parigi 2004)). Should we conclude therefore that most persons are \'93\loch\f41 \hich\f41 disconnected\'94\loch\f41  and experience little sociability (McPherson et\~\hich\f41 
al. 2006; Putnam 2000)?  I would suggest that a more theoretically sophisticated understanding of what \'93\loch\f41 sociability\loch\af41\dbch\af31505\hich\f41 \'94\hich\af41\dbch\af31505\loch\f41 \hich\f41  is all about suggests otherwise. \'93
